# Learner Git — Gitea decision (authoritative)

When authoring or editing Showroom labs, Software Templates, PipelineRuns, seed overlays, or learner scripts:

## Decision (must follow)

1. **Lab / GitOps install starts Gitea** and creates student **user accounts** only (not per-user app repos).
2. **Operator seed** publishes a **public** org **`workshop-templates`** with **public** repos learners and scripts may clone (monorepo isolation — operators may clone GitHub; students never do).
3. **Learners** create their own org **`lw-<username>`** and empty repos, then seed from `workshop-templates` (Module 2 / `learner-seed-from-templates.sh`).
4. **Username-specific URLs** belong in **workshop steps** (ConfigMap `demo-userinfo-gitea`, Showroom `@@LW_USER@@`, `sed` / env substitution) — **never** hardcode `user1`, `lw-user1`, or catalog-only names in seeded trees.

## Hard bans (learner-facing)

- **Never** instruct students to `git clone` / fork / push `https://github.com/NA-FSI-Services/lightwell-tssc-workshop.git` (or any GitHub fork of this monorepo).
- **Never** ask learners to `cd charts/components/spring-boot-lw-poc/app` inside a monorepo checkout.
- **Never** hardcode `lw-user1`, `user1/spring-boot-lw-poc`, or claim-specific hosts in seed overlays, `.tekton` examples, or Software Template defaults meant for all learners.
- **Never** put the GitHub monorepo URL in PipelineRun `repo-url`, copy-paste clone steps, or RHDH publish targets aimed at students.

## Required patterns

| Concern | Pattern |
|---------|---------|
| Template org | `workshop-templates` (`template_app_repo_url`, `template_gitops_repo_url`) |
| Learner org | `lw-<username>` (`student_gitea_org`) |
| App repo | `lw-<user>/spring-boot-lw-poc` → `student_repo_url` |
| GitOps repo | `lw-<user>/gitops-spring-boot-lw-poc` → `student_gitops_repo_url` |
| PipelineRun repo-url | `STUDENT_REPO_URL_PLACEHOLDER` → Module 6 substitutes `student_repo_url` |
| Clone dest | `/tmp/spring-boot-lw-poc` (`pom.xml` at root) |

Use ConfigMap `demo-userinfo-gitea`: `gitea_url`, `student_gitea_org`, `student_username`, `student_password`, `student_repo_url`, `student_gitops_repo_url`, `template_*`.

RHDH `publish:gitea` **requires** a Gitea Organization — owner is `lw-<username>`, not a normal user account.

## Operator-only (OK)

GitHub monorepo URLs are allowed in: root-app / AgnosticV GitOps, Gitea seed Job `SOURCE_REPO_URL`, Showroom content sync, Chart.yaml `home`, agent docs telling operators what **not** to give students.

See `AGENTS.md` (**Learner Git — Gitea first**), `charts/components/gitea/README.md`, issue #120.
